+NOMROM — SKRAPER INTEGRATION AND TORBOX DIAGNOSTICS
+Windows build candidate 1.10.3+24, based on NOMROM 1.10.2+23
+Prepared 2026-11-03
+
+WHAT THIS CANDIDATE ADDS
+
+Settings > Metadata > Skraper provides two explicit tools:
+
+1. Choose gamelist.xml
+   Import an existing Skraper game list, its descriptive fields and its local
+   artwork into NOMROM. Select the matching catalog platform, review the
+   preview and notices, and then import. A ScreenScraper account is not needed
+   for this workflow. Turn on Metadata in Settings to use and display it.
+
+2. Identify local ROM
+   Choose one extracted ROM or disc image. NOMROM streams its bytes to compute
+   CRC32, MD5 and SHA-1 without loading the whole file into memory. The results
+   can be copied. Online matching is a separate, explicit action using the
+   existing ScreenScraper account configuration and approved NOMROM app access.
+   Only filename, size, selected platform and fingerprints are submitted; the
+   ROM file itself is not uploaded. The result is displayed for review and is
+   not automatically written into the catalog or used to rename a file.
+
+IMPORT WORKFLOW
+
+- Export an EmulationStation-style gamelist.xml with Skraper and keep the local
+  images referenced by the XML available.
+- Open Settings, enable Metadata, and choose Skraper > Choose gamelist.xml.
+- Select the matching NOMROM platform explicitly.
+- Set the meaning of the generic <image> field. The default is unclassified
+  artwork, suitable for mixed-image composites. Choose Cover only if these
+  images really are box covers, or Screenshot if they are screenshots.
+- Explicit <boxart>/<box> fields are covers; <screenshot> is a screenshot.
+  Screenshots and mixed artwork are not promoted into fallback box covers.
+- The normal permitted image location is the gamelist's folder and children.
+  For absolute paths or relative references outside that folder, explicitly
+  choose an image folder. This grants a boundary for the referenced files;
+  it does not rewrite or guess broken paths after moving a Skraper export.
+- Preview shows game/image references, skipped entries and unresolved paths.
+  Shared image bytes are saved once, so the final saved-image count can be
+  smaller than the preview's reference count.
+- Import saves a private local index and copies supported artwork. The source
+  XML and original images remain available to Skraper.
+- Remove imports clears the local overlay and its referenced owned image
+  copies. Existing catalog entries, downloaded games, accounts, remote metadata
+  cache and source Skraper files are outside this operation.
+
+HOW RESULTS APPEAR
+
+The existing game details and artwork views read the local results alongside
+their remote metadata. Matching is scoped to the selected platform. Known
+release tags can match across regions; demos and meaningful edition qualifiers
+remain distinct. Ambiguous aliases return no local match rather than choosing
+an arbitrary game. Catalog-provided covers keep their existing first priority.
+Explicitly imported covers precede remaining remote cover candidates. The
+existing Libretro, Wikipedia and optional artwork providers are preserved.
+
+Imported fields stay outside the expiring remote cache. Removing an import
+therefore removes its overlay immediately, without a two-week stale local
+description or image path remaining in the network cache. Imported artwork
+uses an internal URI resolved through the existing image cache; it does not
+require an HTTP server or a network request.
+
+ROM IDENTIFICATION SCOPE
+
+Fingerprints represent exactly the selected file. The tool does not silently
+strip ROM headers, concatenate disc tracks, combine multi-disc games, unpack
+archives, or execute files. ZIP/7z/RAR and common compressed containers must
+be extracted first. Cue sheets and playlists require selecting their data
+file instead. Cancellation discards partial fingerprints, and detected file
+changes during reading produce a retry message.
+
+Online lookup uses ScreenScraper's jeuInfos.php endpoint through NOMROM's
+existing request lane, quotas, secure settings and response handling. A
+verified result requires the correct system, at least one returned matching
+checksum, no contradictory returned checksum, and a matching size if given.
+A filename-only suggestion is not labelled checksum-verified.
+
+NOMROM's approved ScreenScraper application credentials were not available in
+this session. Existing source records say authorization is pending. This
+candidate keeps that setup requirement and does not include Skraper's vendor
+credentials. Local imports and fingerprint calculation remain usable. No live
+ScreenScraper login or known-game request was performed for this candidate.
+
+TORBOX / MINERVA FAILURE CHANGE
+
+The reported symptom was an almost-immediate error with TorBox selected:
+"Not cached on debrid and torrents are disabled". Archive sources worked.
+
+The prior resolver returned null for several distinct outcomes, including
+provider authorization failures, permanent API errors, uncached results,
+file-selection failures and timeouts. The download layer then replaced them
+with the same generic message whenever local torrents were disabled.
+
+This candidate carries a bounded, sanitized failure message and code from the
+provider to the particular download task. It distinguishes invalid credentials,
+plan/size/active limits, unmatched or ambiguous torrent files, cache preparation
+timeouts, network failures and actual uncached results. Cancellation and changed
+credentials do not publish a stale failure for another task.
+
+TorBox progress polling reuses a validated account-and-infohash torrent
+registration. It coalesces simultaneous registration attempts and avoids
+posting createtorrent for every progress poll. Matching prefers normalized
+full paths, then suitable path suffixes, then an unambiguous basename and size.
+An explicit path mismatch cannot fall back to an unrelated positional file.
+
+The immediate timing helps distinguish the report from the normal three-minute
+wait, but it does not establish the actual server/account failure. No TorBox
+account or live MiNERVA torrent was accessed in this session. The new task
+message is needed to identify that remaining condition. Native peer-to-peer
+torrent support remains governed by the existing platform implementation.
+
+VALIDATION AND WINDOWS BUILD
+
+See SKRAPER-VALIDATION.txt for the exact checks completed for this candidate.
+The project dependency versions and hashes remain pinned to the published
+lockfile; xml and crypto only changed from transitive to direct dependencies.
+
+The current deliverable is source, not an updated Windows portable executable
+or installer. Build and verify on a Windows x64 host with the pinned Flutter
+SDK and the existing scripts/build-windows.ps1 and scripts/package-windows.ps1.
+WINDOWS.md describes the native build requirements. Use the account-free build
+unless approved NOMROM ScreenScraper access is supplied through the existing
+private publisher configuration. Do not label a release ScreenScraper-enabled
+until its documented live access checks succeed.
+
+The Windows build candidate uses 1.10.3+24 so it is distinguishable from the
+existing 1.10.2 installation. This version assignment does not publish a
+release or change the automatic update feed. See WINDOWS-CANDIDATE.txt for
+the continuing Windows build and verification record.
+
+IMPLEMENTATION MAP
+
+lib/services/skraper/              Local store, provider, file fingerprints
+lib/widgets/skraper_*              Preview/import/settings controls
+lib/widgets/rom_identification_dialog.dart
+lib/services/game_metadata_service.dart  Local overlay and lookup entry points
+lib/services/game_artwork_cache.dart     Owned local artwork bridge
+lib/services/metadata/screenscraper_provider.dart  Optional checksum lookup
+lib/services/debrid/torbox_provider.dart           TorBox registration/matching
+lib/services/debrid_service.dart                  Failure propagation
+lib/services/download_service.dart                Per-task diagnostics
+test/skraper/                                     Integration regression fixtures
+test/debrid/                                      Debrid regression fixtures
+
+SOURCE PROVENANCE
+
+Published source archive:
+https://github.com/MM-482/NOMROM-Releases/releases/download/v1.10.2/NOMROM-1.10.2-windows-source.zip
+SHA-256:
+ad13561aa0e7f6796c9b107d88c641b3c4c92f280a4104e41f18d7eaf4356756
+
+The native Dart integration was implemented in NOMROM's own architecture.
+The recovered Skraper .NET projects are provided separately for inspection;
+NOMROM's source package does not depend on the recovered WinForms executable.
+Existing NOMROM/Romgi attribution and release instructions are retained.
