+NOMROM 1.10.3+24 — WINDOWS BUILD CANDIDATE
+
+This continues the Skraper integration and TorBox diagnostics source candidate
+previously validated on Linux. The application changes are based on the
+published Windows 1.10.2+23 source archive. Version 1.10.3+24 distinguishes this
+candidate from the installed release while native Windows validation proceeds.
+
+The Windows CI route reconstructs the reviewed source from the exact published
+1.10.2 source archive and the candidate patch. It verifies the archive digest,
+patch digest and every changed file, then invokes the existing Windows build,
+test, package and payload verification scripts on a Windows 2022 x64 runner.
+
+ScreenScraper application access remains unconfigured/pending. The CI workflow
+does not load private publisher keys or personal service credentials, perform
+live TorBox/ScreenScraper calls, publish a release or update the signed feed.
+
+This preparation note does not claim a successful native build. The final
+Windows verification report records the actual run and artifact results.
